  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Musharaka: Oxfam V&#xe4;stsahara</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Musharaka: Youth-led community development in the Sahrawi refugee camps - Western Sahara Oxfam Musharaka project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The contribution will support Oxfam Solidarit&#xe9; to implement their project Musharaka: Youth-led community development in the Sahrawi refugee camps.&#xa0; In the Letter of Appropriation to Sida for 2018 an assignment was included to support the local situation in Western Sahara under the Strategy for Sustainable Peace 2017-2022. The main objective of the project is to improve the role of youth in community development in the Sahrawi refugee camps. The specific objective is to strengthen the capacities and self-confidence of youth, and their recognition as active participants in community development, by the authorities and other stakeholders.
Main objective: to improve the role of youth in community development in the Sahrawi refugee camps
Specific objective: Strengthening the capacities and self-confidence of youth, and their recognition as active participants in community development, by the authorities and other stakeholders
Result 1: The five taskforces, selected through a participative and inclusive process, are functional, and are aware of their responsibility towards the community.
Result 2:&#xa0;Community taskforces have completed a cycle of training and improved their technical skills
Result 3: Youth, as an important part of the taskforces,&#xa0;have developed and successfully implemented inclusive and sustainable projects that respond to the needs of the community
Result 4: Local authorities and taskforces have developed a relationship of trust.
Since the community projects under result 3 will be designed during the implementation the results framework will be updated by Oxfam when their focus have been agreed. The updated results framework will be submitted to Sida for approval&#xa0;as stipulated in the agreement.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Detta projekt kommer att till&#xe4;mpa en s&#xe5; kallad &quot;community driven development approach&quot; d&#xe4;r befolkningen i de fem v&#xe4;stsahariska flyktingl&#xe4;gren kommer att bilda kommitt&#xe9;er (d&#xe4;r minst 50 % &#xe4;r ungdomar och minst 50 % &#xe4;r kvinnor) som kommer att samr&#xe5;da med befolkningen i l&#xe4;gren, myndigheter och andra intressenter f&#xf6;r att definiera behov och sedan utforma projekt som m&#xf6;ter samh&#xe4;llets behov. Ungef&#xe4;r 15 miljoner kronor kommer att tilldelas dessa sub-projekt och syftet med tillv&#xe4;gag&#xe5;ngss&#xe4;ttet &#xe4;r att skapa en h&#xf6;g grad av lokalt &#xe4;garskap, att &#xe5;tg&#xe4;rda en del av behoven f&#xf6;r f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttrade samh&#xe4;llstj&#xe4;nster i l&#xe4;gren samt ge ungdomar en plattform f&#xf6;r att visa att de kan bidra till samh&#xe4;llsutvecklingen. Ett antal utbildningar och workshops f&#xf6;r kommitt&#xe9;rna kommer &#xe4;ven att organiseras som en del av projektet. 

Projektet kommer att genomf&#xf6;ras av Oxfam Solidarit&#xe9;. Oxfam har arbetat med situationen med v&#xe4;stsahariska flyktingar sedan 1975 och &#xe4;r s&#xe5;ledes en av de &#xe4;ldsta humanit&#xe4;ra akt&#xf6;rerna i l&#xe4;gren och har med tiden skaffat sig legitimitet och respekt hos flyktingarna och myndigheterna.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project will apply a community driven development approach where the community in the five Sahrawi refugee camps will form taskforces, with at least 50 % youth and 50 % female representation, that will consult with the community, authorities and other stakeholders to define needs and then design projects that address the community needs. Approximately 15 MSEK will be allocated for these community projects. The intention with the approach is to create a high degree ownership, help address some of the social service needs in the camps and provide an avenue for young people to demonstrate their contribution to community development. A comprehensive training and workshop package will also be provided to the taskforces to enable the implementation of the project.

The project will be implemented by Oxfam Solidarit&#xe9;. Oxfam has been working on the Sahrawi refugee situation since 1975 and is therefore one of the oldest humanitarian actors in the camps and has over time gained legitimacy and respect among the community and authorities.</narrative>
  </description>
